    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (79.32) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.97) anchor the lineup as our elite offensive engines. **Corbin Carroll** is a primary target despite facing Mahle; his elite speed profile provides a necessary floor for our SB-starved roster, and the projected +6% platoon advantage helps mitigate the risk of the matchup. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime position to over-perform his base projection due to a significant +14% park factor and an ideal platoon setup against Alcantara, making him the highest-ceiling play on the board. **Max Muncy** (70.70) rounds out the top tier, benefiting immensely from a generous +17% SP skill boost against Lauer, which vaults him well ahead of his peers in the utility spot.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (44.65), who remained just outside the active cut due to a punishing -9% platoon penalty in a same-handed matchup against Alexander. While **Travis Bazzana** offered the allure of a lead-off spot, the efficiency gap between him and **Jose Caballero**\u2014despite **Jose Caballero**'s own platoon struggles\u2014was deemed sufficient to leave him on the pine to preserve our limited game caps. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Zach McKinstry**, whose 49.23 score is buoyed by his stolen base potential; however, his -3% order penalty and the sub-4.00 xERA of Weathers suggest a high risk of an early pinch-hit substitution if he fails to produce in his initial plate appearances. Overall, the lineup is optimized to chase high-leverage counting stats while maintaining the speed-first identity that defines our pursuit of a 5x5 title.",
